{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 13, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the harsh sunlight assaulting his eyes. He sat up in bed, a strange stiffness in his limbs, and looked around. His bedroom wasn't quite right. The colors were too vibrant, the furniture too perfectly arranged. A notification box, translucent and shimmering, floated in his vision: \"Welcome to Aethelgard! Level 1. Quest: Retrieve the Sunstone.\" He yelped, scrambling back against the headboard. A menu materialized before him, displaying stats like \"Strength: 8,\" \"Agility: 6,\" and \"Health: 100/100.\" This couldn’t be happening. He pinched himself, hard, but the feeling was undeniably real. He was inside a video game. A ridiculously cliché fantasy RPG, no less. He glanced at his hands, noticing they were no longer the familiar flesh and bone, but smooth, almost unnaturally perfect, with a faint, glowing outline.\n\n***\n\nPanic warred with a strange sense of detached curiosity. A wooden door, intricately carved with images of griffins and dragons, stood open at the end of his room. He hesitantly approached, the floorboards creaking with an unnerving precision. A small, pixelated creature with oversized ears and a perpetually worried expression hopped into view. \"Greetings, Adventurer!\" it squeaked. \"I am Pip, your guide. The village elder requests your assistance immediately. The Shadow Blight is spreading, and only you can stop it!\" Arthur stared at Pip, then at the door, then back at the notification box. He took a deep breath. He had no idea what he was doing, but apparently, he was supposed to save a village from a Shadow Blight. He stepped through the door, ready or not, into the unknown world of Aethelgard.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.15061697363853455}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.4355137050151825}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0002076410164590925}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.072171099